 initial sync. The final token/config swap is serialized behind any active sync, so an older request
 cannot restore superseded authorization.
 
+If a previous installation has lost server authorization, including after its account is deleted,
+`connect` reconciles that 401 or 403, removes the stale local authorization and automatic state, and
+starts fresh pairing without requiring `disconnect`. The installation identity and local source
+registry remain stable so discovery and source history can be reused. Other reconciliation failures,
+such as transient server or network errors, retain the existing connection and do not start pairing.
+If auxiliary cleanup cannot finish, the revoked authorization is still removed and the connector
+prints a warning for the remaining local cleanup.
+
